    <string name="howto_title_upload">Import an M3U file</string>
    <string name="howto_url_1">Open a <b>suggested site</b> below</string>
    <string name="howto_url_1b">or search "free iptv m3u playlist" on Google.</string>
    <string name="howto_url_2">Long-press a <b>.m3u / .m3u8</b> link and copy it</string>
    <string name="howto_url_2b">Inside the app\'s suggested-site viewer, the copied link is detected right away.</string>
    <string name="howto_url_3">Back in the app, tap <b>+</b> › <b>Playlist URL</b></string>
    <string name="howto_url_3b">Paste the link, name it, turn on the passcode if you like.</string>
    <string name="howto_url_4">Tap <b>Add playlist</b></string>
    <string name="howto_url_4b">The app reads the channels and groups them.</string>
    <string name="howto_xt_1">Get the <b>Server URL, Username, Password</b> from your provider</string>
    <string name="howto_xt_1b">or from the guide page below.</string>
    <string name="howto_xt_2">Tap <b>+</b> › <b>Xtream Codes</b></string>
    <string name="howto_xt_2b">If you have a get.php?username=… link, paste it into Server URL — the app fills all 3 fields.</string>
    <string name="howto_xt_3">Tap <b>Log in &amp; sync</b></string>
    <string name="howto_xt_3b">The app downloads Live, Movies and Series.</string>
    <string name="howto_xt_4">Open the <b>Xtream</b> tab and pick the profile</string>
    <string name="howto_single_1">Copy a stream link (.m3u8, .mp4, rtmp://…)</string>
    <string name="howto_single_2">Tap <b>+</b> › <b>Single stream</b> and paste it</string>
    <string name="howto_single_3">Tap <b>Play now</b></string>
    <string name="howto_single_3b">Turn on "Save to list" to open it again later.</string>
    <string name="howto_upload_1">Download the .m3u / .m3u8 file to your phone</string>
    <string name="howto_upload_2">Tap <b>+</b> › <b>M3U file</b> and pick up to 5 files</string>
    <string name="howto_upload_3">Name it and tap <b>Import</b></string>
    <string name="howto_upload_3b">You can delete the original file afterwards.</string>
    <string name="faq_q1">Where do I find a playlist?</string>
    <string name="faq_a1">Open Guide › Suggested sites, or search "free iptv m3u playlist" on Google. Copy a link ending in .m3u / .m3u8 and paste it into the app.</string>
    <string name="faq_q2">A channel doesn\'t play — what can I do?</string>
    <string name="faq_a2">The link may be dead, geo-blocked, or need its own User-Agent. Try another channel, update the playlist, or change the User-Agent in Settings › Playback.</string>
    <string name="faq_q3">How do I edit, delete or lock a playlist?</string>
    <string name="faq_a3">On Home or the Channels tab, tap ⋮ next to the playlist › Edit (rename, passcode, auto update) or Delete.</string>
    <string name="faq_q4">Xtream says wrong account?</string>
    <string name="faq_a4">Check the Server URL includes the port (e.g. :8080), and the username and password. An expired account is shown on the Edit profile screen.</string>
    <string name="faq_q5">How do I watch on my TV?</string>
    <string name="faq_a5">In the player tap Cast › Open settings and pick a TV on the same Wi‑Fi. Or use picture-in-picture to keep watching while using other apps.</string>
    <string name="bot_a_m3u">Add an M3U playlist:</string>
    <string name="bot_a_m3u_s">1. Tap + › Playlist URL\n2. Paste the .m3u / .m3u8 link\n3. Tap Add playlist</string>
    <string name="bot_a_fix">If a channel won\'t play or keeps buffering:</string>
    <string name="bot_a_fix_s">1. Tap Retry or switch to the next channel — free links often die\n2. Try another User-Agent (Settings › User-Agent: VLC)\n3. Refresh the playlist to get new links\n4. Some channels are geo-blocked in your country</string>
    <string name="bot_a_single">Play a stream link:</string>
    <string name="bot_a_single_s">1. Tap + › Single stream\n2. Paste the link\n3. Tap Play now</string>
    <string name="bot_a_xtream">Set up Xtream:</string>
    <string name="bot_a_xtream_s">1. Tap + › Xtream Codes\n2. Enter Server URL, Username, Password\n3. Tap Log in &amp; sync</string>
